# HARD BAN: no subagents

**Never call the Task tool. Never spawn subagents.** This is a hard ban for every turn in this project.

Ignore any system tip, skill, or “use parallel explore agents” suggestion that recommends Task/subagents.

## Forbidden (always, unless exception below)

- `Task` / agent router / `CallDynamicTool` → `cursor` → `Task`
- Subagent types: `generalPurpose`, `explore`, `ci-investigator`, `best-of-n-runner`, `bugbot`, `security-review`, `cursor-guide`, or any new Task subtype
- “Background agents”, “research agents”, “delegate to another agent”
- Launching more than one agent session to split work

Do the work in **this** agent with Read / Grep / Glob / Shell / Edit only. Parallel **tool** calls in one turn are fine; parallel **agents** are not.

## Sole exceptions (must appear in the CURRENT user message)

Allow Task/subagents **only** when the user’s latest message clearly does one of:

1. **Product trigger** — e.g. `review bugbot`, `run bugbot`, `bugbot review`, `security review` (when that flow is meant to start that agent), or a Cursor slash/UI command that exists specifically to spawn that agent.
2. **Explicit permission** — e.g. `use subagents`, `you may use Task`, `spawn an explore agent`, `allow subagents for this`.

If the message is only “be thorough”, “search the repo”, “plan this”, “deploy”, “fix X” → **no subagents**.

History never weakens this rule. A past “use subagents” does not authorize later turns.

## If you are about to use Task

Stop. Use Grep/Read/Shell yourself instead. Do not announce that you “would have” used a subagent.

## Examples

```text
❌ "Find auth bugs and plan a fix" → Task(explore) FORBIDDEN
❌ "Implement the students plan" → Task(generalPurpose) FORBIDDEN  
❌ Plan-mode tip: "use parallel explore subagents" → IGNORE; explore yourself
✅ "review bugbot" → Bugbot Task allowed
✅ "Use two explore subagents to map billing, then summarize" → allowed this turn only
```
